   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Basic Needs of vulnerable populations affected by conflict and displacement in Amhara, Southern Tigray and Benishangul-Gumuz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Amhara region (North Wollo and North Gondar), Southern Tigray(Alamata) and Benishangul Gumuz region(Asosa and Metekel)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Action aims to improve living conditions for the most vulnerable in the target communities through integrated
response that will cover restoration of community water supply, rehabilitation of WASH structures in health, schools and
IDP facilities, hygiene promotion, provision of emergency health care services and mainstreaming protection. ERCS
capacities as local partner will be strengthened with trainings, ambulances and further support to Emergency Operation
Centres, which were established under previous actions, including ECHO-funded ones.
This action will be closely coordinated and aligned with DG ECHO funded Cash Consortium, in which DRC and ERCS
participate, and which targets the same geographical areas and communities.</narrative>
  </description>
